{# Decision template: who carries the scene on when the player presses Continue Narration, as one choice over the
   legal (speaker, target) pairs the game enumerated. The player says nothing new; someone present simply speaks
   next. Rendered into a decisions request, never into chat messages. Sent when
   dialogue.decisions.useForSpeakerSelection is on; otherwise, or without a usable answer, the game picks the last
   speaker, else the NPC in the crosshair, else the nearest.

   Context set by the game: decision_pairs (key, speakerUUID, speakerName, targetKind, targetUUID, targetName),
   decision_speakers (UUID, name, distance, isVirtual, isPrivateVirtual), triggeringEvent (the continue request),
   crosshairTarget, lastSpeaker, lastDialogueTarget, events, maxRecentEvents. The virtual-NPC rules and no
   self-target are already applied to the pairs. Keys are short and numbered per request (s2_tplayer, s2_t5); use
   p.key as given. There is no none option: someone always speaks.

   A criterion is one line; profiles and other multi-line decorators belong in the state blocks. #}
{% set ss = get_speaker_selector_settings() %}
{% set tagCompanion = ss.tagCompanion %}
{% set tagEngaged = ss.tagEngaged %}
{% set tagInScene = ss.tagInScene %}

[ state last_exchange ]
{% if existsIn(lastSpeaker, "name") and existsIn(lastDialogueTarget, "name") %}
{{ lastSpeaker.name }} spoke last, to {% if lastDialogueTarget.UUID == player.UUID %}{{ player.name }}{% else %}{{ lastDialogueTarget.name }}{% endif %}.
{% else if existsIn(lastSpeaker, "name") %}
{{ lastSpeaker.name }} spoke last, to no one in particular.
{% else %}
No one has spoken yet.
{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ state recent_dialogue ]
{{ render_template("components\\event_history_compact") }}
[ end state ]

[ state looking_at ]
{% if crosshairTarget and crosshairTarget.UUID and crosshairTarget.UUID != 0 %}
{{ player.name }} is looking at {{ crosshairTarget.name }} ({{ units_to_meters(crosshairTarget.distance) }}m away).
{% else %}
{{ player.name }} is not looking at anyone in particular.
{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ state location ]
{{ location }}
[ end state ]

[ state nearby ]
{% for c in decision_speakers %}
{% set cinfo = decnpc(c.UUID) %}
{{ cinfo.name }}{% if existsIn(lastSpeaker, "UUID") and lastSpeaker.UUID == c.UUID %} [SPOKE LAST]{% endif %}{% if cinfo.isVirtual %} (virtual NPC){% else %} ({{ cinfo.gender }} {{ cinfo.race }}, {{ units_to_meters(c.distance) }}m away){% endif %}{% if tagCompanion and is_follower(c.UUID) %} [COMPANION]{% endif %}{% if tagEngaged and is_in_package(c.UUID, "SkyrimNet_PlayerFollowPackage") %} [ENGAGED]{% endif %}{% if tagInScene and ((is_plugin_loaded("SexLab.esm") and is_in_faction(c.UUID, "SexLabAnimatingFaction")) or (is_plugin_loaded("OStim.esp") and is_in_faction(c.UUID, "OStimExcitementFaction"))) %} [IN SCENE]{% endif %}
- {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", c.UUID) }}
{% endfor %}
{% if tagCompanion or tagEngaged or tagInScene %}
Tags: {% if tagCompanion %}[COMPANION] is the player's active follower. {% endif %}{% if tagEngaged %}[ENGAGED] is already in conversation with the player. {% endif %}{% if tagInScene %}[IN SCENE] is physically occupied in an intimate scene. {% endif %}
{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ question next choice ]
{{ player.name }} has asked the scene to continue without saying anything. Decide who speaks next and to whom.
`last_exchange` says who spoke last and to whom; `recent_dialogue` is the conversation so far, oldest first.
By default the person marked [SPOKE LAST] carries on, to the same person: they finish a thought, follow up, press a point or react to the silence. Choose someone else only when the scene clearly calls for them: they were just asked something and have not answered, they were just addressed by name, or the last line was plainly their cue.
When no one has spoken yet, prefer the person {{ player.name }} is looking at, then a companion, then whoever is closest.
Choose an option where the speaker addresses another NPC only when the recent dialogue is between them, or the speaker clearly has something to say to that NPC.
[ criteria ]
{% for p in decision_pairs %}
{{ p.key }}: {{ p.speakerName }} speaks next, to {% if p.targetKind == "player" %}{{ player.name }}{% else %}{{ p.targetName }}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
